dwm - dynamic window manager
============================
dwm is an extremely fast, small, and dynamic window manager for X.


Requirements
------------
In order to build dwm you need the Xlib, Xinerama, Xft, FreeType, and
fontconfig development headers. The active configuration also expects
Kitty, Rofi (preferred; dmenu is kept as a fallback), `xprop`, `wpctl`,
`brightnessctl`, and the JetBrains Mono Nerd Font.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (dwm is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install dwm (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running dwm
-----------
Add the following line to your .xinitrc to start dwm using startx:

    exec dwm

In order to connect dwm to a specific display, make sure that
the DISPLAY environment variable is set correctly, e.g.:

    DISPLAY=foo.bar:1 exec dwm

(This will start dwm on display :1 of the host foo.bar.)

In order to display status info in the bar, you can do something
like this in your .xinitrc:

    while xsetroot -name "`date` `uptime | sed 's/.*,//'`"
    do
    	sleep 1
    done &
    exec dwm


Configuration
-------------
The configuration of dwm is done by creating a custom config.h
and (re)compiling the source code.


Custom features in this checkout
--------------------------------
This checkout uses the fullgaps layout patch (for tiled and monocle
layouts) and adds the following bindings:

* Gruvbox dark colors are used for DWM, the bar, and Rofi.
* Tag 9 uses a Zen-like bullseye glyph; `Alt+9` still selects it.
* The bar is drawn directly by DWM with an opaque full redraw, padded modules,
  and a focus accent; `~/.local/bin/dwm-status` supplies its memory, volume,
  battery, and clock text.
* `Alt+M` zooms the focused client; `Alt+Shift+M` selects monocle.
* `Alt+minus` and `Alt+equal` change the current monitor's gap size.
  Runtime gaps are capped at 100 pixels; `Alt+Shift+equal` removes them.
* `Alt+Return` starts Kitty, `Alt+P` opens Rofi (falling back to dmenu),
  and the audio/brightness keys use PipeWire (`wpctl`) and `brightnessctl`
  respectively. Rofi starts in `drun` mode; `Ctrl+Tab` switches modes.
* `Alt+Q` closes the focused window; `Alt+Shift+Q` quits dwm.

`config.h` is the active configuration. `config.def.h` is the tracked
starting point for creating a new configuration. The matching Rofi theme is
stored at `~/.config/rofi/config.rasi`. It is intentionally centered,
rectangular, icon-free, and currently 15% transparent to match dmenu. On
Arch, install the preferred launcher with:

    sudo pacman -S rofi

Keep `config.h` backed up or tracked separately; it is intentionally not
ignored. Rebuild after changing it:

    make clean all

Install the resulting binary system-wide with:

    sudo make install

The source already includes the gap implementation. The
`patches/dwm-fullgaps-6.8.diff` patch is based on upstream commit
`44dbc6809d05b8f2addc483f882e670db0b6b8e9` and reproduces the gap/layout
changes only (including the safer gap/runtime configuration); copy or
recreate `config.h` separately when applying it to a clean checkout. The
older 6.4 patch is kept for reference.
